From a4ffa32c9876d34a655b1954eacdb3e107639ef7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cedric Hauber <hauber.c@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 14:08:34 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(runout): print the filament left in the path after a
 spool runout

On a type-B MMU whose entry sensor sits before the gear (QIDI Box), a runout paused as
soon as the end of the filament cleared the entry sensor, then unloaded it with the gear.
By then the end may already be past the gear: the unload cut the filament and nothing
could pull the rest back, so it stayed in the bowden.

With runout_use_remaining the print goes on with what is left in the path, like the QIDI
stock firmware. The runout is the end clearing the extruder entry sensor: the toolhead
parks for the runout, the rest is pushed out through the nozzle (past the extruder gears,
the piece below is left for the next load like a cut fragment), then EndlessSpool loads
the next gate or the print pauses until the tool is loaded again. A toolchange or unload
in the meantime pushes the remains out the same way, without cutting: a cutter above
the extruder gears would leave the upper piece with nothing to move it.

The state is read from the sensors (loaded, gate entry sensor clear), so it holds after a
restart or once the print has ended. While it lasts FlowGuard is off, the shared exit
runout is ignored, and the loaded check and pause recovery accept the empty gate and hub.
Needs mmu entry and extruder entry sensors and no encoder. Default 0: unchanged.

The test filament model now opens a switch when the end of a run-out filament passes it
moving forward.
